.TH PATCHSPLIT 1 "August 2026" "patchsplit 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
patchsplit \- download a GitHub pull request patch and split it by commit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patchsplit
.RI < owner/repo > " <pr-number>"
.RS
[\c
.B \-\-out
.IR dir ]
[\c
.B \-\-force ]
.RE
.br
.B patchsplit
.RI < owner > " <repo> <pr-number>"
.RS
[\c
.B \-\-out
.IR dir ]
[\c
.B \-\-force ]
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B patchsplit
downloads the patch for a GitHub pull request and splits it into
individual patch files, one for each commit.
.PP
The resulting patch files are written to the
.B patches
directory by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-out " " \fIdir\fR
Write split patch files to
.IR dir .
The default is
.BR patches .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite existing patch files.
By default, existing files are not overwritten.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B patchsplit rust-lang/rust 12345
Download and split pull request 12345 from
.BR rust-lang/rust .
.TP
.B patchsplit openai codex 42 \-o pr-42-patches
Download pull request 42 from
.BR openai/codex
and write the resulting patches to
.BR pr-42-patches .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.B patchsplit
uses
.B curl
to download pull request patches from GitHub.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1)
